From 3676b7824e738377dece6ec998ae0c7d99ca20ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:12:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Fix simulator inconsistencies with the thesis model

- Same random seed for baseline and enhanced runs (identical sites/UEs)
- Baseline small cells use one 400 MHz carrier (was 800 MHz)
- Thermal noise uses the serving layer bandwidth (was fixed 400 MHz)
- Wall loss only for indoor UEs; indoor state fixed per UE
- TR 38.901: PL_NLOS = max(PL_LOS, PL'_NLOS); UMa NLoS sigma 6 dB
- PF equal share with the 60 Mbps GBR floor of Eq. 3.12 (enhanced)
- 6G: 1024-QAM SE cap, passive RIS (no 15 dB amplifier gain),
  60 GHz oxygen loss, near-field mirror bound on cascaded gain
- Plots: SE CDF and Tput-vs-SINR use simulator outputs; synthetic
  slice plot disabled; CSO reference script labelled honestly and
  side-lobe level measured beyond the first null

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011doGnc1MmrMsyjZpDL7kbW
